JIANT FM V10.61 – studio twin (firmware code for the host), built from https://github.com/juanjiant-bit/JIANT commit 6c48e2a8e7049c31ab77c57b97c3ef6790d24090
(source: https://github.com/juanjiant-bit/JIANT/archive/6c48e2a8e7049c31ab77c57b97c3ef6790d24090.tar.gz; JIANT has no tags: V10.61 is the version this commit reports).
GPL-3.0-only. JIANT FM by juanjiant-bit, a fork of Felucca: Copyright (C) 2026 Leo Kuroshita (@kurogedelic), Hügelton Instruments (Felucca), and JIANT's authors (its changes and additions).
Ported parts keep their licences (msfa in fm6_core.c: Apache-2.0; the UI faces Chakra Petch, Inter Tight and Michroma and the Fukiai icons are rasterised in: OFL 1.1, MIT; VOICE's English words are a subset of the CMU Pronouncing Dictionary: BSD-2-Clause):
JIANT's LICENSING.md and the texts in THIRD_PARTY.txt beside this file. The Bluetooth stack, the USB host and the JieLi SDK files of JIANT's packages are not part of the twin.
The firmware sources are unmodified. The glue tools/studio/jiant_studio.c (GPL-3.0-only, in FM-1 Companion's source) includes them as JIANT's own browser emulator and host tests do (web/emu/felucca_web.c, tests/hostsim.c,
editor_test.c, backup_test.c) and replaces only the hardware: keys/LEDs/LCD, ADC (MASTER; battery full), NOR flash = a 1 MiB RAM image, USB = always configured (SysEx and MIDI out through usb.c's rings),
one core, no 320 MHz switch, no supply setup, no Bluetooth, no USB host, no USB audio (the INPUT engine hears silence), no TRS MIDI, no serial console, no updater (ota.c answers the identity handshake only).
Compiled with WASI SDK clang (include shim tools/wasm_shim/sys/wait.h).

Corresponding Source (GNU GPL 3.0, section 6)
